# History: United States

In this course, we want to learn a story. We want it to be a true story but also a story that keeps our minds engages and shows how we got to where we are today. The story being told is that of the United States, starting from before its first inhabitants.

The course is divided into 4 quarters of 8 weeks each, where each week has 4 days worth of instruction. Each week, there will be different ways of learning (e.g., videos, articles, activities, etc.), but it's up to you to follow along and truly learn.

### Course Outline
* Quarter 1
  * Early inhabitants (1 week)
  * Early European settlers (2 weeks)
  * 13 Colonies (2 weeks)
  * The American Revolution (3 weeks)
* Quarter 2
  * The Constitution (1 week)
  * Early United States (3 weeks)
  * Civil War (3 weeks)
  * Reconstruction (1 week)
* Quarter 3
  * Westward Expansion (2 weeks)
  * Industrialization (1 week)
  * World War 1 (3 weeks)
  * The Great Depression and the New Deal (1 week)
* Quarter 4
  * World War 2 (3 weeks)
  * Cold War (3 weeks)
  * Civil Rights Movement (1 week)
  * Modern Times (1 week)

**Textbook:** The textbook for the course is [U.S. History from OpenStax](https://openstax.org/books/us-history/pages/1-introduction).
